 I, n: usize) -> Option<I::Item>"},{"DocComment":" where"},{"DocComment":"     I: Iterator,"},{"DocComment":" {"},{"DocComment":"     let next = iter.next();"},{"DocComment":"     if n > 1 {"},{"DocComment":"         iter.nth(n - 2);"},{"DocComment":"     }"},{"DocComment":"     next"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Panics"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The method will panic if the given step is `0`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let a = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5];"},{"DocComment":" let mut iter = a.into_iter().step_by(2);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some(0));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some(2));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some(4));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self"},{"index":1,"name":"Clause0_Item"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"data":{"file_id":2,"beg":{"line":1,"col":0},"end":{"line":1,"col":0}},"generated_from_span":null},"origin":"TraitSelf","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":12,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":17367},{"Deduplicated":17368}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":17367},{"Deduplicated":1160}],"output":{"HashConsedValue":[17476,{"Adt":{"id":{"Adt":49},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":17367}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}]}},"src":{"TraitDecl":{"trait_ref":{"id":12,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":17367},{"Deduplicated":17368}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}},"item_id":{"Method":7}}},"is_global_initializer":null,"body":"Opaque"},null,{"def_id":102,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["iter",0]},{"Ident":["traits",0]},{"Ident":["iterator",0]},{"Ident":["Iterator",0]},{"Ident":["zip",0]}],"span":{"data":{"file_id":40,"beg":{"line":629,"col":4},"end":{"line":632,"col":24}},"generated_from_span":null},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" 'Zips up' two iterators into a single iterator of pairs."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `zip()` returns a new iterator that will iterate over two other"},{"DocComment":" iterators, returning a tuple where the first element comes from the"},{"DocComment":" first iterator, and the second element comes from the second iterator."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" In other words, it zips two iterators together, into a single one."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If either iterator returns [`None`], [`next`] from the zipped iterator"},{"DocComment":" will return [`None`]."},{"DocComment":" If the zipped iterator has no more elements to return then each further attempt to advance"},{"DocComment":" it will first try to advance the first iterator at most one time and if it still yielded an item"},{"DocComment":" try to advance the second iterator at most one time."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" To 'undo' the result of zipping up two iterators, see [`unzip`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`unzip`]: Iterator::unzip"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Basic usage:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let s1 = \"abc\".chars();"},{"DocComment":" let s2 = \"def\".chars();"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut iter = s1.zip(s2);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some(('a', 'd')));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some(('b', 'e')));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some(('c', 'f')));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Since the argument to `zip()` uses [`IntoIterator`], we can pass"},{"DocComment":" anything that can be converted into an [`Iterator`], not just an"},{"DocComment":" [`Iterator`] itself. For example, arrays (`[T]`) implement"},{"DocComment":" [`IntoIterator`], and so can be passed to `zip()` directly:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let a1 = [1, 2, 3];"},{"DocComment":" let a2 = [4, 5, 6];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut iter = a1.into_iter().zip(a2);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some((1, 4)));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some((2, 5)));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some((3, 6)));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `zip()` is often used to zip an infinite iterator to a finite one."},{"DocComment":" This works because the finite iterator will eventually return [`None`],"},{"DocComment":" ending the zipper. Zipping with `(0..)` can look a lot like [`enumerate`]:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let enumerate: Vec<_> = \"foo\".chars().enumerate().collect();"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let zipper: Vec<_> = (0..).zip(\"foo\".chars()).collect();"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!((0, 'f'), enumerate[0]);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!((0, 'f'), zipper[0]);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!((1, 'o'), enumerate[1]);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!((1, 'o'), zipper[1]);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!((2, 'o'), enumerate[2]);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!((2, 'o'), zipper[2]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If both iterators have roughly equivalent syntax, it may be more readable to use [`zip`]:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::iter::zip;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let a = [1, 2, 3];"},{"DocComment":" let b = [2, 3, 4];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut zipped = zip("},{"DocComment":"     a.into_iter().map(|x| x * 2).skip(1),"},{"DocComment":"     b.into_iter().map(|x| x * 2).skip(1),"},{"DocComment":" );"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(zipped.next(), Some((4, 6)));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(zipped.next(), Some((6, 8)));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(zipped.next(), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" compared to:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" # let a = [1, 2, 3];"},{"DocComment":" # let b = [2, 3, 4];"},{"DocComment":" #"},{"DocComment":" let mut zipped = a"},{"DocComment":"     .into_iter()"},{"DocComment":"     .map(|x| x * 2)"},{"DocComment":"     .skip(1)"},{"DocComment":"     .zip(b.into_iter().map(|x| x * 2).skip(1));"},{"DocComment":" #"},{"DocComment":" # assert_eq!(zipped.next(), Some((4, 6)));"},{"DocComment":" # assert_eq!(zipped.next(), Some((6, 8)));"},{"DocComment":" # assert_eq!(zipped.next(), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`enumerate`]: Iterator::enumerate"},{"DocComment":" [`next`]: Iterator::next"},{"DocComment":" [`zip`]: crate::iter::zip"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self"},{"index":1,"name":"U"},{"index":2,"name":"Clause0_Item"},{"index":3,"name":"Clause1_Item"},{"index":4,"name":"Clause1_IntoIter"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"data":{"file_id":2,"beg":{"line":1,"col":0},"end":{"line":1,"col":0}},"generated_from_span":null},"origin":"TraitSelf","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":12,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":17367},{"Deduplicated":17384}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},{"clause_id":1,"span":{"data":{"file_id":40,"beg":{"line":632,"col":11},"end":{"line":632,"col":23}},"generated_from_span":null},"origin":"WhereClauseOnFn","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":22,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":